Manage the cache settings of a distribution (admin:ManageCache, docs/11 §11.1):
its defaults, the overrides of a domain (--domain) and of the paths a pattern
selects (--behavior). The settings are inherited from the cluster ("nexoctl
cache settings") to the distribution, the domain and the path; every level may
name a policy ("nexoctl cache policy") and override its fields.

Usage:
  nexoctl dist cache [flags]
  nexoctl dist cache [command]

Available Commands:
  export      Export the cache settings of a distribution as YAML
  import      Replace the cache settings of distributions with those of a YAML file
  set         Change the cache settings of a distribution, a domain or a path
  show        Show the cache settings of a distribution and the effective policy of its domains

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for cache

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl dist cache [command] --help" for more information about a command.
